return {
  summary = "Gold Gen 2 voxel/Stadium 2 mod with visible-only roaming encounters by default.",
  author = "Stadium Overworld Models Gen 2 port",
  tags = { "gen2", "gold", "silver", "stadium2", "voxel", "3d", "overworld", "standalone" },
  differences = {
    changed = {
      "uses Gold's current engine-owned render_pipelines drawWorld world pass when available, with render.compose retained as the legacy/mobile fallback",
      "uses game.data.gen2Encounters / world.encounters with MORN-DAY-NITE Gold tables",
      "uses the embedded Gen-2 renderer and embedded Gen-2-patched Wilds runtime as authoritative standalone components",
      "Stadium pack loading accepts National Dex 1-251",
    },
    added = {
      "v0.2.77 splits 3D POKéMON MODELS from 3D PLAYER MODEL so Stadium Pokémon and the Character Selector human player can be toggled independently",
      "v0.2.76 gives Gold dialogue and YES/NO prompts the same translucent Stadium glass UI and adds configurable 2.2x/4x/8x/12x OPEN WORLD diorama zoom limits plus an official zoom.range whole-region survey rung",
      "v0.2.75 fixes BATTLE COMMANDS layout collisions by reserving separate command/footer lanes and makes Pokédex/party Stadium previews fit current animated pose bounds against both horizontal and vertical FOV so full 3D models remain visible",
      "v0.2.74 makes the custom Gold battle command UI appear automatically, arms direct shortcuts only after the command panel has actually rendered, auto-pages only ordinary intro prompts, and prevents a held intro button from selecting an unseen first command; connected outdoor seams now reattach the preserved Wilds trailer during map.entered for a flicker-free outdoor follower handoff",
      "v0.2.73 restores the moving Wilds follower as Gold slot 1, suppresses and cleans stale native Gen-2 follower copies instead of deleting the active trailer, and makes LEAD PARTY FOLLOWER gate the Wilds trail itself",
      "v0.2.72 fixes Gold follower duplication across zone/map transitions by making the native Gen-2 follower authoritative for slot 1, reserving Wilds trailers for follower 2+, and purging orphan native follower copies",
      "v0.2.71 restores visible roaming wild Pokemon under the current Gen1Recomp sandbox by moving Wilds file probes to mod/engine-safe APIs",
      "v0.2.70 restores current Gen1Recomp sandbox compatibility, re-enables the supported Gold drawWorld voxel pipeline, and automatically uses render.compose when red_3d_player / 3D Character Selector is installed so its selected skin/camera pipeline remains live",
      "v0.2.69 restores the confirmed v0.2.45 desktop render.compose/canvas-exit behavior across Voxel3D, ShadowMap and AntiAlias, keeps Android/iOS nested-canvas restoration, and disables the still-broken v0.2.68 desktop drawWorld experiment",
      "v0.2.67 fixes fresh desktop/fresh-options voxel mode: Gold native TILT=OFF now uses the normal 35-degree voxel diorama while 3D VOXEL WORLD is ON instead of flattening the camera; TILT 15/35/50 stay literal and voxel OFF remains native 2D",
      "v0.2.66 restores the proven v0.2.45 live ChunkMesher for actual voxel terrain and removes VoxelDiskCache from the live mesher dependency path, fixing the regression where the game could fall back entirely to Gold 2D even with disk cache disabled",
      "v0.2.65 fixes Stadium ROM import crashes on current sandboxed Gen1Recomp builds by delegating platform detection, save-directory I/O, desktop HostShell staging, and mobile native picking to engine-owned APIs; Android/iOS N64 picks are validated and fed directly to StadiumInstall instead of touching blocked love.system/love.filesystem/io paths",
      "v0.2.64 is a boot-recovery release: post-v0.2.45 optional UI/settings installers fail closed, Android whole-frame patching is Android-only, mod-option persistence no longer replaces global ManagerState persistence, and persistent voxel disk-cache I/O is quarantined",
      "v0.2.63 restores the stable Stadium UI preview render order after v0.2.62 caused a real-runtime crash, and gives the extra-tall Pokedex viewer safe headroom by moving the camera aim instead of probing live rig vertices; v0.2.61 follower/settings fixes remain",
      "v0.2.60 adds a live CUSTOM UI / MENUS toggle that returns pause/submenus/Mod Manager/live-battle UI to Gold originals without disabling voxel features, and makes the Pokédex 3D viewer taller while retaining v0.2.59 model scale",
      "v0.2.57 fixes full Pokédex scrolling and prevents OPEN WORLD stitched-map overlaps from visually replacing the current map/collision layout; voxel disk-cache geometry revision is refreshed for terrain-art correctness",
      "v0.2.56 organizes this mod's long settings page into category submenus, writes every Gen-2 mod option immediately to Loader's top-level persistent modOptions store, and makes Android FLIP SCREEN 180 DEGREES rotate the entire Game2 frame plus touch input",
      "v0.2.55 adds persistent FULL voxel terrain disk caching for faster repeat OPEN WORLD loads, fixes Gen-2 mod-settings persistence across restart, and adds live Stadium 2 3D model previews to the custom POKéDEX list/entry pages",
      "v0.2.54 makes Gold OPTIONS TILT control the real voxel camera pitch and keeps the live overworld visible behind pause-launched OPTIONS/POKéDEX/POKéMON/PACK/POKéGEAR/AJ/SAVE glass menus",
