      "v0.2.50 fixes live-battle trainer grounding: the displaced battle trainer is vertically pinned to the real encounter ground and battle mode clears stale walk/ledge lift so the trainer cannot float above raised scenery",
      "v0.2.47 makes OPEN WORLD a literal full-3D world: every connected map uses full voxel meshes with seam masking and an outer voxel apron, OPEN WORLD itself keeps the voxel provider active, and far maps warm incrementally without forcing the scene back to flat 2D",
      "v0.2.46 fixes OPEN WORLD so it extends the normal voxel/Stadium renderer instead of falling back flat: voxel terrain, 3D trees/grass/props and Pokemon models stay active, and the ON/OFF toggle now invalidates residency live",
      "v0.2.45 adds an optional OPEN WORLD mode: OFF keeps current-map + direct-neighbour streaming; ON background-loads and retains the entire cardinally connected Gold overworld graph as one continuous voxel world, with live OFF cleanup and fail-safe fallback",
      "v0.2.44 makes BATTLE COMMANDS a full UI switch: ON uses the custom Stadium battle HUD; OFF restores Gold's original Gen-2 battle UI and native battle controls",
      "v0.2.42 fixes the 3D Pokémon Party/Stats runtime path and adds the same animated Stadium 2 model preview to the live battle PKMN and item-target party selectors",
      "v0.2.41 adds a live animated Stadium 2 model showcase to the pause-launched custom POKéMON party screen and its STATS/Summary pages, with a slow showroom turn plus matching HP/moves/stat presentation and safe Egg/missing-model fallbacks",
      "v0.2.40 turns MODS into a matching Stadium-style submenu chain and applies the same Mod Manager/detail/options presentation to every installed mod using the standard manager/options_schema flow, with safe auto-skinning for conventional list-like third-party START menus",
