      "v0.2.38 targets Gold's real src.ui.gen2.StartMenu and renders it with the exact custom PACK/PKMN battle-selector language (four-row glass panel, matching highlights/footer and MENU ACCOUNT help panel) while preserving Gold's native actions/input",
      "v0.2.36 adds an Android camera-slider visibility toggle and a full-frame 180-degree reverse-landscape screen flip",
      "v0.2.32 replaces the normal live Gold battle canvas with a full controller-native window HUD (HP/name panels, message panel, controller command diamond and custom move selection) while Gold battle logic stays authoritative",
      "v0.2.32 moves battle visibility clearing into the actual live Gold VoxelScene and hard-cuts tall trees/walls/bushes/grass/flowers from the arena and camera-to-Pokemon sight corridors while preserving the ground",
      "v0.2.29 adds smart live-battle sightline dissolve for blocking trees/walls/shrubs, a controller-diamond command UI (Square Fight / Circle Run / Cross Pack / Triangle PKMN), PC arrow shortcuts, WASD Pokemon movement and visible right-stick battle camera control",
      "v0.2.27 adds direct 3D Pokemon control in Gold battles: left stick moves the active Stadium model around the arena and PlayStation Square / Xbox X triggers imported Stadium 2 skeletal attack performances with a following battle camera",
      "v0.2.26 keeps Lugia world-space attacks centered by pinning its torso/root while preserving its imported Stadium skeletal motion; Gold move presentation remains latched independently of AnimRunner swaps",
      "v0.2.23 makes Gold ordinary trainer fights use the same live 3D/Stadium battle staging as wild encounters instead of falling back to the flat native scene",
      "v0.2.23 bridges Gold BattleState:animForMove into the real imported Stadium 2 skeletal clip bank and pairs those motions with the world-space 3D move FX",
      "v0.2.22 restores the original Stadium 2 Lugia: diagnostics proved its 647-vertex main body is intentionally textureless, so Dex 249 now renders the 0xFFFF texture sentinel as an opaque white lit material instead of skipping the body",
      "v0.2.20 bypasses the unstable Stadium 2 Dex-249 ROM hierarchy entirely and gives Lugia an isolated fully 3D procedural rescue model, so Lugia fixes can no longer break the other 250 Pokemon",
      "v0.2.19 adds DSM4/DSM5 cache compatibility and isolates experimental Stadium 2 node-flag transforms to Lugia instead of applying them to the whole roster",
      "v0.2.16 introduces DSM5 packs that preserve Stadium geo joint transform flags and replays the source mixed scale/TRS paths so Lugia can assemble from its real 3D model instead of hierarchy guesses",
      "v0.2.15 restores Lugia to a real Stadium 2 3D model with runtime hierarchy repair and opaque body textures, and makes overworld Poké Ball throws substantially harder with strength-scaled aim windows, faster precision timing, stricter throw grades, and visible off-target ball flight",
      "v0.2.13 gives Lugia a species-correct opaque world-card fallback instead of the translucent/wrong generic roaming sprite while corrupt Dex-249 Stadium 2 geometry remains rejected",
      "v0.2.13 bridges real continuous 3RD/1ST displacement into the 3D Character Selector walking pose only during rendering, so player animations work without spoofing Gold gameplay movement",
      "v0.2.12 separates Poké Ball aim from throw: hold L2/right mouse for the shoulder camera, then R2/left mouse throws without any automatic Ball use",
      "v0.2.12 adds LOW-to-EXTREME capture resistance from Gen-2 base stats plus encounter level while preserving Gold Ball/catch rules",
      "v0.2.11 makes capture a pre-contact R3/right-click throw from the camera cone and polls Gold input.step so it works while standing still",
      "v0.2.11 uses a dedicated UV-sphere Poké Ball prop/material instead of the scrambled COLLADA atlas mapping",
      "v0.2.10 makes overworld capture reliable through the native Wilds battle-start seam, adds direct C/right-shoulder/right-trigger entry, real mouse clicks, multi-Ball inventory support, and a Poké Ball mesh fallback",
      "v0.2.09 adds dedicated world-space Aeroblast and Sacred Fire signature effects on top of the Gold AnimRunner-powered 3D effect bridge",
      "v0.2.09 adds Gen-2 legendary overworld presence scaling for Raikou, Entei, Suicune, Lugia and Ho-Oh while keeping Celebi naturally small",
      "v0.2.08 wires Gold's real Gen-2 AnimRunner move id/attacker/frame into the world-space Stadium-style 3D attack-effect renderer and adds more Gen-2 signature aliases",
      "v0.2.07 removes Gold's duplicate native 2D player trainer back-sprite from live voxel battle intros, leaving the already-present 3D trainer as the only trainer presentation",
      "v0.2.06 adds a direct-overworld 3D Poké Ball aim/throw/shake capture minigame for visible wild Pokémon, using the supplied ball model and Gold catch/storage structures",
      "v0.2.05 adds resilient desktop F6 camera cycling plus mapped-controller right-stick look in both 3RD and 1ST person while preserving mouse look",
      "v0.2.04 streams each directly connected Gold map as real voxel terrain one area ahead in every available cardinal direction for seamless route/town handoffs",
      "v0.2.03 doubles the real outdoor round-tree apron to 32 tiles per side and makes the smart live battle camera crash-safe on LuaJIT/LÖVE",
      "v0.2.01 adds smooth continuous diorama pinch/wheel camera-distance zoom and an optional Stadium-style smart orbit camera for live-world battles",
